{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1002849-help-with-legacy-rules","id":1002849,"title":"Help With Legacy Rules","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-14T05:55:37-08:00","id":1002849,"title":"Help With Legacy Rules","content":"I am trying to figure out in the new rules set how one builds a reality stalker as I am currently lost at the moment.<br /> <br /> Thanks","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12406-hobbes","name":"Hobbes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T06:10:32-08:00","id":1002856,"title":"","content":"What particularly are you having trouble with?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T06:31:44-08:00","id":1002862,"title":"","content":"legacy powers as I am not sure how to determine them as the only legacy with a full write up that I have found in the book was the 11th question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12406-hobbes","name":"Hobbes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T06:39:28-08:00","id":1002864,"title":"","content":"There's an explanation for how attainments should be constructed in the legacy section.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T06:38:19-08:00","id":1003904,"title":"","content":"Old school legacies often end up stretched out in ways you might not expect. The 1e first attainment will likely fit 1st &amp; 2nd in 2e, for example, but don't be shocked if you end up going higher. The second and third attainment map, I find, most often to 4th &amp; 5th. (Dreamspeakers are going to be a challenge.)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> There is room for a number of powers, but the reach requirements make it odd. <br /> <br /> <br /> Anything that was always-on used to be Indefinite duration and often reflexively restored. In the new rules, the closest would be advanced duration and Instant casting time. That's two Reach, right there. If you need sensory range, that's another. <br /> <br /> <br /> A lot of sensory spells target the caster, so you don't need Sensory range on those. For anything you want sympathetic, you'll need to add Sensory casting range.<br /> <br /> <br /> A 1st level effect gets one reach per level of attainment. That reduces by one per level of spell. (just another way of looking at it)<br /> <br /> <br /> Some nice stuff hides behind Reach, so don't expect to pick an effect from each level of the arcana to populate the list. As indicated, you'll often need the final two attainmentss to duplicate the original effects (3&amp;4 dot effects in 4th &amp; 5th att. get 2 Reach, and 1 Reach. In 5, they get 3 &amp; 2 Reach) <br /> <br /> <br /> It's not rare that there is no way to duplicate an effect with the new rules. A translation, then, has to be willing to break the rules or reimagine the legacy.<br /> <br /> <br /> Hopefully, that helps.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T11:58:55-08:00","id":1004040,"title":"","content":"Reality Stalkers in particular are going to be difficult as sympathetic range requires a reach by itself. If I had to do it, I would axe the pocket dimension aspect entirely (leave that for outside of the attainments) and do something like the following:<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">First Attainment: </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Correspondence - with instant cast time</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Optional: Mental Scan - with instant cast time</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Second Attainment: </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Break Boundary - with instant cast time</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Optional: Alter Mental Pattern - with instant cast time</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Third Attainment:</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Ward - with instant cast time and advanced duration</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Optional: Cost: 1 Mana - Incognito Presence with instant cast time and advanced duration, may be used on items instead of the mage himself.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Fourth: Attainment: </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: 1 Mana</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Scrying with instant cast time, sympathetic range, and advanced duration</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Optional: Imposter, with instant cast time and advanced duration</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Fifth Attainment: </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: 1 Mana</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Teleportation with instant cast time and sympathetic range</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Optional: Hallucination, with instant cast time and advanced duration<br /> <br /> This preserves the Reality Stalkers as sneaks (both physically sneaky and sneaking into peoples' minds). Someone else can chime in with why this is a terrible adaptation but I don't think it's a terrible starting point for your own 1E-&gt;2E conversion.</span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My ideas are bad and I should feel bad.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark","name":"Kvark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}